// has a layer for the vowel it says shows that layer instead of the half-open or open mouth.
// The vowel comes from the voice's lip track (below), which kagex-lipsync makes for the voices
// a game picks; the layers go by these names, in English or in kana. A mouth group needs
// "Closed Mouth" and either the half-open and open mouths or at least one vowel.
// A voice without a track opens and shuts its mouth by loudness alone, unless lipEngineVowels
// is set: then the engine's WaveSoundBuffer.getVowel picks a vowel, but it mostly hears how
// high the voice is, not what it says (UPSTREAM.md)
